    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0389" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.00/1393.</note>
                <head>[Extract]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    national elections were held in this country on Sunday, Monday, and Tuesday, the
                    29th to 31st ultimo, inclusive. Gen. Manuel Bonilla and Dr. Francisco Bográn are
                    declared to have been chosen President and Vice President, respectively.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles D. White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
